sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If two numbers, multiplied by one another make some number, and any prime number measures the product, then it also measures one of the original numbers.
----
proof:

Let the two numbers {A} and {B} multiplied by one another make {C}, and let any prime number {D} measure {C}.

I say that {D} measures one of the numbers {A} or {B}.

